A||||15||ramzy_steele||Subs behind the seat||||1||
Z||000000||ramzy_steele||03-20-2001||12:17 PM||||I knwo this topic has been on here before and i thought i saw someone do it behind the seats.  However I am getting shipped 2 12" huyge subs and a 1400 watt amp and im selling my T/A for a fiero.  Can i fit these things anywhere?  Thanks for the help.  Also is the 88 fiero fomula much better then any other years or is it just the name basically?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-20-2001||12:27 PM||||Don't know anything about the subs, but the Fiero Formula was similar to the Firebird Formula.  Both were stripped models with the best suspension/tires/drivetrain setup.  No fastback/aero stuff on the Formulas.  Basically, it was your generic coupe with the 2.8 and WS6 suspension (which is overrated, IMHO).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Johnson's85SE||03-20-2001||12:44 PM||||Hi,<BR> I think the biggest problem you will encounter will be the length of the 12" woffers. I have two ten inch subs behind my seats, and without cutting holes into the firewall, I am uncomfortable. Take the length of the woffer and add the thickness of the wood, and the distance of throw the woffer will move. It will be quite a lot of space, but still do able. <P> My seat is only one notch back from all the way forward. I am 5'10 but will sacrifice some comfort for my sound. Where do you plan on mounting the amp? I have mine on one of the boxes, but would like to relocate, without major modifications. <P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||7
Z||000003||FieroLisa||03-20-2001||01:02 PM||||I have my subs behind my seat- but I am 5'2" so the need to have my seat all the way up to fit the sub is fine, since I need it all the way up to reach the pedals!  <P>I have a 10 inch sub in a custom box made to fit behind my seat with it all the way forward. I have my amp mounted behind the passenger seat, at least until I get the cash to buy another sub.<P>If you are tall and don't the steering wheel up your nose when you drive, you can put a box and sub in the passenger footwell, or put one sub behind the passenger seat and mount the amp behind your seat.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ramzy_steele||03-20-2001||01:06 PM||||crap im 6'3 any ideas to mount these beast somewehre?||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||03-20-2001||01:09 PM||||places ive seen them mounted:<BR>passenger footwell<BR>behind passenger seat/driver seat<BR>an 8 in. will fit in your center console glovebox<BR>in the spare tire compartment (but that will rattle)<P>beyond that, be creative!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||03-20-2001||01:25 PM||||with two 12s and you being 6'3" i think you're sh!t outta luck. unless you put quite a bit of money into it you can make a custom enclosure in the front compartment and have everything sealed off so it doesn't rattle. then you would have to build a port that goes into the passenger compartment. someone has done that and they have site showing how they did it. i forgot the link though.<P>if i were you, i would get rid of one of them and make a box behind the passenger seat. or keep them to use in a different car. besides, why do you need two 12s in a fiero??<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||03-20-2001||01:49 PM||||Here's what folks are talking about with the footwell install. It's a fiberglass enclosure with wood face. I am currently reproducing some of these right now. (AkursedX, just finished the fiberglass shell for yours today, should be ready for shipping by the end of the week) Cost is $150 w/o driver. Uses a 10" low Q sub.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high"> <BR>I gotta say, 2 12's is kinda overkill. With just the 10", I get a LOT of crisp bass. Just a thought.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ramzy_steele||03-20-2001||02:06 PM||||You kave no idea how much overkill these things are.  1000 watt subs and 1400 watt amp.  Anyway that idea baouthe fornt compartment and sending tubes into my car sounds interesting.  Anyone knwo the address or have pics or anyhthing?||||reg||1
Z||000009||sqoach||03-20-2001||02:27 PM||||here's a link to what i was talking about:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/%7elunapark/</A> <P>and the custom sub install is not the only thing this guy's done. his fiero is killer!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Johnson's85SE||03-20-2001||02:45 PM||||I also had two tens in my back window, with plexiglass on the front and back, mdf on the sides and top and bottom. When I used the back window, I got to keep most of the room, but them created more blind spots in the car. I drove of a year and a half with it, something you just get used to. I also had a twelve behind the passanger seat. I look kinda silly, with one seat all the way back, and the other all the way ahead. We also made a tiny box, to fit in the spare tire well, with the same twelve. Without porting it into the car, it is a waist of time. I got more attention from the people outside of my car, than from the passanger. Just some Ideas. <BR>Cheers!<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||03-20-2001||03:12 PM||||also, here is fierosound's sub install<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <P>he has a 12 behind each seat. he used really shallow subs though. if yours are pretty deep, this might not work as good.||||reg||1
